      ],
      "notes": "Replaces Gemini CLI (command: agy). Detected by its own folder (~/.gemini/antigravity-cli), by the shared config folder (~/.gemini/config), or by the folder of the agy launcher the Antigravity app installs (%APPDATA%/Antigravity/bin on Windows): the app and the CLI share these, so the app alone can show it as installed. Paths are from Google's Antigravity CLI docs (settings, skills, MCP, instructions) and are best-effort. A conversation log is the transcript.jsonl of each conversation; its fields are not documented, so it is shown as text and no token usage is read. Hooks are read from ~/.gemini/config/hooks.json and .agents/hooks.json (format from Google's docs: named hooks with events and an optional enabled flag); plugins are not listed yet. Token usage is not in the transcript files: reports place it in the conversations' SQLite databases as protobuf, an internal format, so it is not read. The CLI's /usage command shows your quota."
